WEBVTT

00:00:09.839 --> 00:00:11.049
- (grunts)
- (Lucy) Edmund!

00:00:11.132 --> 00:00:13.885
You all right? Oh!

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:15.219
(Lucy laughing)

00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:19.599
(growls) Huh!

00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:35.865
Beards and bedsteads!

00:00:36.908 --> 00:00:38.785
Maybe that horn worked after all.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.912
What horn?

00:01:00.681 --> 00:01:03.559
(male) This bread is so stale.

00:01:03.643 --> 00:01:07.105
(male 2) I'll just give him some soup.
He should be coming around soon.

00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:09.440
(male) I don't think
I hit him hard enough.

00:01:09.524 --> 00:01:11.192
(male 2) Nikabrik, he's just a boy.

00:01:11.275 --> 00:01:15.655
He's a Telmarine, not some lost puppy.
You said you were gonna get rid of him.

00:01:15.738 --> 00:01:19.242
No. I said I'd take care of him.

00:01:19.325 --> 00:01:22.620
We can't kill him now.
I just bandaged his head.

00:01:22.703 --> 00:01:25.623
It would be like murdering a guest.

00:01:25.706 --> 00:01:28.084
How do you think his friends
are treating their guest?

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:31.712
Trumpkin knew what he was doing.
It's not the boy's fault.

00:01:33.172 --> 00:01:34.590
Ah!

00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:37.635
Stop! Stop!

00:01:38.386 --> 00:01:40.430
Hold it. No, no!

00:01:40.513 --> 00:01:43.516
I told you we should have killed him
when we had the chance.

00:01:43.599 --> 00:01:45.101
You know why we can't.

00:01:45.184 --> 00:01:46.853
If we're taking a vote,
I'm with him.

00:01:46.936 --> 00:01:49.021
We can't let him go.
He's seen us.

00:01:49.105 --> 00:01:50.648
Enough, Nikabrik!

00:01:50.731 --> 00:01:52.900
Or do I have to sit
on your head again?

00:01:54.318 --> 00:01:57.238
And you. Look what
you made me do.

00:01:58.239 --> 00:02:00.575
I spent half the morning
on that soup.

00:02:02.076 --> 00:02:03.786
What are you?

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:07.165
You know, it's funny
that you would ask that.

00:02:07.248 --> 00:02:09.667
You think people would
know a badger when they saw one.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.252
No. No, I mean...

00:02:12.753 --> 00:02:16.048
...you're Narnians.
You're supposed to be extinct.

00:02:16.841 --> 00:02:18.384
Sorry to disappoint you.

00:02:21.762 --> 00:02:25.099
Here you go. Still hot.

00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:28.686
Since when did we open a boarding house
for Telmarine soldiers?

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:30.021
I'm not a soldier.

00:02:31.063 --> 00:02:34.775
I am Prince Caspian. The tenth.

00:02:35.735 --> 00:02:37.904
What are you doing here?

00:02:40.072 --> 00:02:41.616
Running away.

00:02:45.411 --> 00:02:48.539
My uncle has always
wanted my throne.

00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:53.836
I suppose I have
only lived this long

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.547
because he did not
have an heir of his own.

00:02:58.966 --> 00:03:03.554
- Oh... That changes things.
- Yeah.

00:03:03.638 --> 00:03:05.848
Means we don't have
to kill you ourselves.

00:03:05.932 --> 00:03:08.226
You're right.

00:03:10.353 --> 00:03:13.189
- Where are you going?
- My uncle won't stop until I am dead.

00:03:13.272 --> 00:03:17.151
But... you can't leave.
You're meant to save us.

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:20.738
Don't you know what this is?

00:03:34.043 --> 00:03:36.254
(rattling)

00:03:48.015 --> 00:03:50.601
You have quite a library, doctor.

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:57.525
Is there anything
particular you seek, my lord?

00:03:57.608 --> 00:04:01.112
I think I've already found
what I'm looking for...

00:04:03.197 --> 00:04:05.992
...in one of my soldiers!

00:04:24.719 --> 00:04:27.888
What do you know
of Queen Susan's horn?

00:04:28.639 --> 00:04:31.309
It was said to be magic.

00:04:31.392 --> 00:04:33.019
Magic?

00:04:33.102 --> 00:04:38.149
The Narnians believed it could summon
their kings and queens of old.

00:04:38.232 --> 00:04:42.695
At least, such was the superstition.

00:04:45.072 --> 00:04:49.452
And what does Caspian
know of this superstition?

00:04:49.535 --> 00:04:54.498
My lord, you forbade me
from mentioning the old tales.

00:04:56.709 --> 00:04:58.836
So I did.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:10.640
I will say this. If Caspian
does know of the Deep Magic...

00:05:10.723 --> 00:05:14.060
...my lord would
have good reason to be nervous.

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:30.785
First our prince...

00:05:31.619 --> 00:05:33.204
...now his tutor.

00:05:33.287 --> 00:05:36.457
If the members of Miraz's
own house are not safe,

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.877
- are any of us?
- (man) Lord Sopespian!

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.880
Those are dangerous words,
Lord Sopespian.

00:05:42.963 --> 00:05:45.716
But these are
dangerous times, general.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:50.805
One should choose his words as carefully
as he chooses his friends.

00:05:55.768 --> 00:05:58.938
How long until
the bridge is finished?

00:05:59.021 --> 00:06:02.233
- Construction continues on schedule.
- That's not good enough.

00:06:02.316 --> 00:06:04.860
I need my army
across that river now.

00:06:04.944 --> 00:06:08.072
May I suggest you contribute
some of your own men?

00:06:08.155 --> 00:06:10.282
I've only so many at my disposal.

00:06:10.366 --> 00:06:13.869
A fact you'd be wise to remember.

00:06:15.996 --> 00:06:17.581
Go to Beruna.

00:06:17.665 --> 00:06:22.002
Take as many troops as you need.
We must get to Caspian before they do.

00:06:22.837 --> 00:06:24.630
"They," my lord?

00:06:24.714 --> 00:06:28.467
It's time you learned your history.

